    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.notify for example\n\n### Description\n\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/14fa445f-f503-4d66-b4f9-e82f25eaff9c)\r\n\r\nNo problem with manually downloading such demos and using mpv or other player but it would be nice to play such demos in Firefox. To convert screencasts from gnome-shell I use ffmpeg wrapped by bash function:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nscreencast_to_yuv_420p ()\r\n{\r\n    declare in out helpMessage;\r\n    helpMessage='screencast_to_yuv_420p in out';\r\n    in=\"${1?${helpMessage}}\";\r\n    out=\"${2?${helpMessage}}\";\r\n    ffmpeg -i \"${in}\" -vf 'pad=ceil(iw/2)*2:ceil(ih/2)*2' -pix_fmt yuv420p \"${out}\"\r\n}\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2024-10-18T10:33:44Z",
