        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hm, after refreshing the video became available, but not sure how often it works. At the moment I then cannot see the error reported in console. In the past Firefox complained about unsupported pixel format (yuv444). \r\n\r\nOn the other side, after manually download https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/24854248/81014300-3380-4b8c-9ab5-ba09345032d7 I see (by `ffprobe`) `yuv420p` format, the same as suggested by me above. I then have no idea what happened. \r\n\r\nMore: I converted this video to pixel format `yuv444p` and FF can play it for me. \r\n\r\nCurrently I use FF 132.0b5 (Developer Edition) on Debian Sid. \r\n\r\nFinally, it seems that this issue can be closed in this form, especially that both pixel formats are supported. \r\n\r\nNonetheless, thanks for attention!",
            "created_at": "2024-10-18T10:33:45Z",
